body:
I think I would prefer this form:

```suggestion
template <typename T, typename T2>
constexpr auto MIN(const T m_a, const T2 m_b) {
		return m_a < m_b ? m_a : m_b;
}

template <typename T, typename T2, typename T3, typename... Rest>
constexpr auto MIN(const T m_a, const T2 m_b, const T3 m_c, const Rest... m_others) {
		return MIN(MIN(m_a, m_b), m_c, m_others...);
}
```

Perhaps even (not sure if that compiles correctly, I'd have to test):
```c++
template <typename T, typename T2>
constexpr auto MIN(const T m_a, const T2 m_b) {
		return m_a < m_b ? m_a : m_b;
}

template <typename T, typename T2, typename... Rest>
constexpr auto MIN(const T m_a, const T2 m_b, const Rest... m_others) {
		return MIN(MIN(m_a, m_b), m_others...);
}
```

The reason being that the original `MIN` / `MAX` are left intact and can be specialized (if needed), while the varargs template only exists to simplify / delegate calls.

